      "is_best": true,
      "html": "<div class=\"post__content post__content--new-editor\"><blockquote><p> I have just lost <strong>two </strong>posts!</p></blockquote><p>Actually, it seems they were not lost.</p><p>The forum discarded them both, but now <strong>both </strong>have appeared!</p><p> </p><figure><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://uploads-eu-west-1.insided.com/stmicroelectronics-en/attachment/f3d66155-d1c9-41e4-9d2e-361b330a36ac.png\"/></figure><p>Here:</p><oembed url=\"https://community.st.com/stm32-mcus-embedded-software-32/nucleo-f446re-modbus-slave-reads-fail-with-truncated-exception-responses-166484?postid=742681#post742681\"></oembed><p> </p><p><em>(I’ve reported one, so it may get removed)</em></p></div>"
    },
    {
      "is_best": false,
      "html": "<div class=\"post__content post__content--new-editor\"><p>After writing a response in a thread, I clicked “Send”, the text from editor disappeared and immediately the red line appeared above the emptied editor pane:</p><figure><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://uploads-eu-west-1.insided.com/stmicroelectronics-en/attachment/d840495b-e47e-4721-b1e0-2137137b2070.png\"/></figure><p>As shown, I did not have the “Leave a reply” text in the editor pane at that moment.</p><p>After reloading the given thread, the post I’ve been just written *was* there, complete as far as I can judge.</p><p>This is rather upsetting.</p><p>JW</p><p> </p></div>"
    },
    {
